WEBVTT

00:23:59.440 --> 00:24:01.416
I want to get people who elevate a team,

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:05.209
who put the organization's mission
above their own individual self-interest.

00:24:05.590 --> 00:24:06.823
How do you do that one?

00:24:06.847 --> 00:24:08.069
Good luck, Cade.

00:24:08.093 --> 00:24:09.355
CM: (Laughs) You're right.

00:24:09.379 --> 00:24:12.263
I agree that that's a huge challenge.

00:24:12.287 --> 00:24:13.518
AG: Yes, victory!

00:24:14.042 --> 00:24:15.201
My work here is done.

00:24:15.225 --> 00:24:17.359
(Laughter)

00:24:17.383 --> 00:24:18.877
CM: Hold on, hold on.

00:24:18.901 --> 00:24:20.924
It's one of the great
challenges in hiring.

00:24:20.948 --> 00:24:23.959
We run into this with sports
analytics all the time now,

00:24:23.983 --> 00:24:25.854
where you're watching,

00:24:25.878 --> 00:24:27.940
you're trying to evaluate
a football player,

00:24:27.964 --> 00:24:29.880
say, he's one of 22 people on the field,

00:24:29.904 --> 00:24:32.004
and so it's really hard to know